[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Accepted"]
[ECO "D27"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "hanging-pawns,quick-development"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 { Black takes the pawn, which cannot be held for long. } 3. Nf3 { Develops a piece and stops ...e5, which would let Black trade queens and keep the pawn. } 3... Nf6
( 3... e6 4. e3 Nf6 5. Bxc4 c5 6. O-O a6 )
4. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1 so it can win the c4 pawn back. } 4... e6 ( 4... c5 5. Bxc4 e6 6. O-O a6 ) ( 4... Bg4 5. Bxc4 e6 6. h3 { Forces the bishop to decide, before it can pin the knight on f3 to the queen. } 6... Bh5 7. Nc3 )
5. Bxc4 { Wins the pawn back with a developing move, so White has a good centre and has lost nothing. } 5... c5
6. O-O a6
7. Qe2 { Prepares Rd1 and guards the bishop on c4 from behind. } 7... b5
8. Bb3 { Keeps the bishop on the diagonal that points at f7. } 8... Bb7
9. Rd1 { Puts the rook behind the d-pawn, ready to answer ...cxd4 with exd4 and press on the d-file. } 9... Nbd7
10. Nc3 *
